meta {
  name: 15a. Cleanup - Delete Pipeline with confirmation
  type: http
  seq: 39
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/pipelines/:id?{{sagaPipelineConfirmation}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{sagaDataSetId}}
  id: {{sagaPipelineId}}
}

tests {
  test("Pipeline deleted", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(204);
  });
}

docs {
  **Saga step 15a** — Delete the Pipeline and confirm the removal.

  The query names every id of the impact from step 15. In one transaction the backend deletes the Pipeline, marks the FROST DataSink `PENDING_UNPROVISION` and deletes the STA API. The next release, or the dataset delete in step 13, removes the FROST project.

  A `204` here also shows that step 15 changed nothing: the Pipeline still existed.

  **Precondition:** step 15 saved `sagaPipelineConfirmation`.

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | Pipeline deleted; FROST DataSink marked `PENDING_UNPROVISION`; STA API deleted |
  | Config Adapter | — |
  | External System | — (storage stays until the next saga) |
}
